  m_text: This was a painting stolen from the Sistine Chapel, presented to me by
    the Pope. It depicts a respectable British citizen, like I, supporting a respectably
    wigged judge upon one long finger. A finer painting, resembling Michelangelo's
    works, I have never seen. The only one to equal it is Moriarty's stolen painting,
    the Mona Lisa. I will soon kill the rascal and recover it.
